WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.376
Preload describes end-diastolic filling and myocardial stretch; the school uses ventricular filling volume as a useful simplified proxy. Afterload describes the load the ventricle must overcome to eject. Stroke volume is the amount ejected with one beat.
前负荷描述舒张末期充盈及心肌牵张，学校用心室充盈量作便于理解的简化指标。后负荷是心室射血必须克服的负载，每搏量则是一次搏动射出的量。

00:00:17.376 --> 00:00:35.928
Cardiac output is heart rate multiplied by stroke volume. A monitor supplies electrical rate, not stroke volume. Therefore a normal rate cannot establish normal output, and a fast rate cannot be interpreted without asking what happened to filling and the amount ejected per beat.
心输出量等于心率乘每搏量。监护提供电心率，不提供每搏量。因此心率正常不能证明输出正常；解释心率快时，也必须问充盈和每搏射出量发生了什么。

00:00:35.928 --> 00:00:56.328
Blood loss can reduce preload and stroke volume, so tachycardia may initially compensate. Poor contractility after myocardial injury can reduce output despite available filling. High afterload can make ejection harder. These mechanisms may coexist rather than fitting a single tidy category.
失血可降低前负荷、每搏量，心动过速可能先进行代偿；心肌损伤后的收缩性差，即使有充盈也可能输出低；高后负荷会增加射血困难。这些机制可能并存，并非总能整齐归类。

00:00:56.328 --> 00:01:15.384
Increasing filling helps only within the heart’s physiological capacity. Excess volume in a failing pump may worsen congestion. Use the mechanism to organize assessment, but do not convert a conceptual preload lesson into an automatic fluid instruction for every hypotensive patient.
增加充盈只在心脏生理容量范围内可能有益；泵衰竭时过多容量可能加重淤血。机制用于组织评估，但不能把前负荷概念课变成所有低血压患者自动输液的指令。

00:01:15.384 --> 00:01:33.840
Sympathetic activation generally raises rate, contractility and AV transmission during pain, stress or shock. Vagal activity can slow sinus activity and AV conduction. The tracing records part of that response; the history helps explain why it occurred.
交感激活通常在疼痛、应激或休克中增加心率、收缩性和房室传导；迷走活动可减慢窦性活动及房室传导。波形记录其中一部分反应，病史则帮助解释为何发生。

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:53.040
Review beta-blockers, calcium-channel blockers, digoxin and other relevant exposures. Vomiting, vagal stimulation or nodal ischemia can also contribute to slowing. A medication history may explain why a very ill patient does not develop the expected compensatory tachycardia.
应复核β受体阻滞剂、钙通道阻滞剂、地高辛等相关暴露。呕吐、迷走刺激或结区缺血也可能使心率减慢；药物史还可解释为何重症患者未出现预期代偿性心动过速。

00:01:53.040 --> 00:02:12.936
Hypoxia can increase electrical instability and worsen myocardial oxygen imbalance. Acid–base disturbance can impair cardiac function and interact with potassium abnormalities. Neither has one mandatory ECG appearance, and a single waveform cannot establish blood gas results.
缺氧可增加电不稳定、加重心肌氧供需失衡；酸碱紊乱可损害心功能，并与钾异常相互影响。二者均没有必须出现的唯一心电形态，不能从一个波形确定血气结果。

00:02:12.936 --> 00:02:34.248
Consider the whole illness: respiratory failure, sepsis, diabetic metabolic disturbance or other causes may affect rhythm. Continue appropriate airway, breathing and circulatory assessment, obtain available measurements and communicate the suspected mechanism without claiming laboratory confirmation that you do not have.
应考虑整个疾病过程：呼吸衰竭、脓毒症、糖尿病代谢紊乱等均可影响节律。继续适当的气道、呼吸、循环评估，取得可用测量，并报告疑似机制，不能声称已有实际上没有的实验室证实。

00:02:34.248 --> 00:02:55.728
The school associates hyperkalemia with peaked T waves, less visible atrial activity and widening QRS, potentially progressing to severe conduction disturbance. These changes are variable and need not appear in a fixed sequence. A dialysis or renal history can sharply increase concern even without textbook waves.
学校把高钾联系高尖 T 波、心房活动不明显及 QRS 增宽，严重时可进展为传导障碍。但变化并不固定，也不一定按顺序出现；即使没有典型波形，透析或肾病史也可显著增加警惕。

00:02:55.728 --> 00:03:17.256
Hypokalemia can produce flat T waves, prominent U waves and ectopy, and may increase repolarization risk. An apparent long interval may partly be a fused T–U complex rather than a clean QT measurement. Communicate the suspicion and measurement limitation rather than diagnosing an exact electrolyte value.
低钾可产生 T 波低平、明显 U 波和异位活动，并增加复极风险。看似延长的间期可能部分来自 T-U 融合，而非清晰 QT。应报告疑虑及测量局限，不能诊断精确电解质数值。

00:03:17.256 --> 00:03:35.688
Hypothermia can slow the heart and conduction, prolong intervals and produce an Osborn or J wave. These are useful clues, not universal requirements or a standalone temperature measurement. Consider exposure, measured temperature and overall physiology together.
低温可使心率、传导减慢，延长间期，并产生 Osborn/J 波。这些是有用线索，不是必备条件，也不是独立体温测量，应结合暴露史、实测体温与整体生理状况。

00:03:35.688 --> 00:03:52.896
Manage the cold patient through the applicable environmental and resuscitation pathway while monitoring changes. Handle the patient appropriately and document the temperature context. Do not force a temperature-related tracing into a routine normothermic rhythm explanation.
应按适用环境急救及复苏流程照护低温患者并监测变化，恰当搬动，记录体温背景。不能把温度相关波形强行套进正常体温下的常规节律解释。

00:03:52.896 --> 00:04:12.864
For each case, propose a mechanism and a finding that would support or weaken it. A volume-loss story, a pump-failure story and a vasodilation story may all produce tachycardia, but they do not justify the same response. ECG is part of that reasoning, not the entire explanation.
对每个案例，提出一种机制及能支持或削弱它的发现。容量丢失、泵衰竭、血管扩张都可能出现心动过速，但不能据此采用相同处置。心电图只是推理的一部分，不是全部解释。

00:04:12.864 --> 00:04:31.272
After an intervention through the authorized pathway, reassess symptoms, pulse, pressure, skin, mentation and the tracing. Improvement in rate without improvement in perfusion is an incomplete response. Record the cause you suspected and the evidence that changed your plan.
按授权流程干预后，应复评症状、脉搏、血压、皮肤、意识及波形。心率改善却灌注未改善，属于不完整反应。记录所怀疑原因，以及改变计划的证据。
